{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"sec-1","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:56af3c7e2758851c18ce1c7cfe419208686d0442345d09615ed71c6050bb11ef/papers/short.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/short?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196","passage_ref":"sha256:a1593370c38e12db1c19bd7e6926ae58ff48cf2267100066f3070a6a2aaeb22c/papers/short.md/sha256:56af3c7e2758851c18ce1c7cfe419208686d0442345d09615ed71c6050bb11ef/papers/short.json/passages/sec-1","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&paper=short&passage=sec-1","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&paper=short&passage=sec-1","span":{"end_byte":36334,"end_line":229,"start_byte":1011,"start_line":29},"stage":"short"},{"anchor":"front","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:c5ef293cf53aeb8f954222f093a487e61ba3fc0e950b89344f6162142b155538/papers/expository.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/expository?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196","passage_ref":"sha256:ac9916d1ac153686a97c543a0407fd5891500f4d75d0a51f0565cca6570236cf/papers/expository.md/sha256:c5ef293cf53aeb8f954222f093a487e61ba3fc0e950b89344f6162142b155538/papers/expository.json/passages/front","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&paper=expository&passage=front","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&paper=expository&passage=front","span":{"end_byte":531,"end_line":5,"start_byte":23,"start_line":2},"stage":"expository"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&view=arguments&node=euler.theorem-1.1&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&node=euler.theorem-1.1&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&node=euler.theorem-1.1&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&view=arguments&node=euler.theorem-1.1&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&ref=sha256%3Ab6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b%2Fnodes%2Feuler.theorem-1.1","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A result as the authors number it. Its links to the Lean were made with AI for Proof Reader and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.euler.theorem-1.1"],"evidence_ids":["link.euler.theorem-1.1"],"id":"euler.theorem-1.1","kind":"goal","label":"Theorem 1.1","locator":"Theorem 1.1, Section 1","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Theorem 1.1.** There is an odd divergence-free $u_0\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb T^3;\\mathbb R^3)$ whose maximal classical solution $u$ of (1.1) is smooth and odd on $\\mathbb T^3\\times[0,T_*)$ for a finite $T_*>0$, and satisfies $$\\begin{equation}\n \\int_0^{T_*}\\|\\nabla u(t)\\|_{L^\\infty}\\,\\mathrm dt=\\infty,\n \\qquad\n \\int_0^{T_*}\\|\\operatorname{curl}u(t)\\|_{L^\\infty}\\,\\mathrm dt=\\infty. \\tag{1.2}\n\\end{equation}$$ Moreover, $$\\begin{equation}\n \\sup_{0\\le t<T_*}\\|u(t)\\|_{L^\\infty}<\\infty,\n \\qquad \\lim_{t\\uparrow T_*}|\\operatorname{curl}u(t,0)|=\\infty. \\tag{1.3}\n\\end{equation}$$ For every compact $K\\subset\\mathbb T^3\\setminus\\{0\\}$ and every integer $m\\ge0$, both $u(t)$ and $\\partial_tu(t)$ converge in $C^m(K)$ as $t\\uparrow T_*$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.theorem-1.1","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50